      "text": [
        "4512 - : وَ سُئِلَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ: ۝ وَ اَلْمُحْصَنٰاتُ مِنَ اَلنِّسٰاءِ ۝\nقَالَ \"هُنَّ ذَوَاتُ اَلْأَزْوَاجِ\" قُلْتُ ۝ وَ اَلْمُحْصَنٰاتُ مِنَ اَلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا اَلْكِتٰابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ ۝ قَالَ \"هُنَّ اَلْعَفَائِفُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4512 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about the saying of Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic: \"And [forbidden to you are] married women\" (Surah An-Nisa 4:24).\nImam (as) said: \"They are those who have husbands.\"\nI said: \"And [lawful in marriage are] chaste women from among those who were given the Scripture before you\" (Surah Al-Ma'idah, 5:5).\nImam (as) said: \"They are the chaste women.\""
        ]
      }
    },
